Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||01-22-2000||07:26 PM||||I've been looking for quite some time now for a good GPS system to run on my laptop. Obviously it is to be used in my Fiero. I don't want a fixed system like Alpine's or Philips' Carin (don't want to give anyone an excuse to break into my car).<P>Problem with most systems I've seen so far is that they're either rediculously expensive or very inaccurate. Not only do I want to be able to view my position on a (moving) map, but I want real-time directions (thus fast auto-routing) as well.<P>Does anyone have any good suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||David||01-22-2000||08:52 PM||||Cliff<P>I saw an advertisement some months ago for mapping software that had the option of GPS.  I'll try to come up with the name of the company.||||reg||1
