Z||000003||2FAST4U||01-22-2000||11:17 PM||||Cliff<P>I've been researching some GPS stuff for my company. One of the following sites should lead you to what you are looking for.<P>The GPS systems in BMW, Audi, Lexus, and Mercedes all use software from a company called Navigation Technologies. I have been unable to locate this company so have no contact info.<P>I have located some interesting hardware and software at the following sites.<P>gpspilot.com - has gps software for the palmpilot w/ scrolling maps<P>trimble.com - a major supplier of gps mapping equipment also has navagation stuff.<P>skydiversdepot.com - all brands of gps navagation stuff<P>datumproducts.com<P>gpsproducts.com<P>teletype.com/gps<BR> <BR><A HREF="http://gauss.ggs.unb.ca/manufact.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://gauss.ggs.unb.ca/manufact.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 01-22-2000).]||||reg||1
